# WS2-05 (temporary drop point), added in Phase 9 from the 9.2.2 verifier's reproduction
# (build/tmp/assessment/verify/ws2/p1/file-temp.clo, session ses_dea9a612affe7B68nL0nJN0bQn).
# Committed after the verifier's run, before this probe's own run. Sources: spec/03 §5
# and spec/decisions.md D5 (temporaries drop at statement end), spec/17 §3 (a temporary
# created anywhere in a statement is dropped at statement end), std.io `File freedBy
# Close` (the drop closes and flushes the file).
# Expected: the temporary File from `mk(...)` is closed at the end of its statement, so
# the five bytes are on disk when the file is reopened: "wrote 5" then "read 5".
# Contrast: the File bound to a local in an inner block (closed at block end) — the same
# output.
profiles: host hosted-amiga
expect: output
contrast: let w: i32 = writeBytes(mk("build/tmp/assessment/WS2/f260.txt"), bytes(data)); ==> let w: i32 = 0;\n    {\n        let f: File = mk("build/tmp/assessment/WS2/f260.txt");\n        w = writeBytes(f, bytes(data));\n    }
contrast-expect: output
--- output
wrote 5
read 5
--- contrast-output
wrote 5
read 5
